WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.858
Every kitchen hears the same question,

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:05.497
every single night.

00:00:05.517 --> 00:00:06.810
What's for dinner?

00:00:08.577 --> 00:00:11.875
In this kitchen, the answer started as a list.

00:00:11.895 --> 00:00:14.083
Every recipe worth making twice.

00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:16.981
Learned over the years, cooked for family,

00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:19.620
and tweaked until it was right.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.332
Pad Thai. Bolognese.

00:00:21.352 --> 00:00:22.786
Chicken Shawarma.

00:00:22.806 --> 00:00:24.877
French Onion Soup.

00:00:24.897 --> 00:00:28.062
The list kept growing. It still does.

00:00:29.346 --> 00:00:31.867
But a list can't tell you what you can cook tonight.

00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:33.874
It doesn't know what's in your pantry.

00:00:33.894 --> 00:00:37.240
And it definitely doesn't know you're out of lemons.

00:00:38.527 --> 00:00:40.604
So the list got a kitchen of its own.

00:00:40.624 --> 00:00:42.657
One part food. One part humor.

00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:45.875
All of it built for feeding the family.

00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:47.973
This is Dueling Kebabs.

00:00:50.115 --> 00:00:53.661
Every dish is on the menu, all in one place.

00:00:53.681 --> 00:00:56.720
Browse the whole collection, filter by cuisine,

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.269
or spin the globe and pick a spot on the map.

00:01:01.654 --> 00:01:02.702
Behind the scenes,

00:01:02.722 --> 00:01:05.001
the staples are already stocked.

00:01:05.021 --> 00:01:07.093
Spices, sauces, rice, noodles,

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:10.510
and the proteins that always live in the freezer.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.300
More than two hundred and fifty of them,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.424
loaded in ahead of time.

00:01:15.444 --> 00:01:18.374
So the site already knows what's on hand.

00:01:20.115 --> 00:01:21.605
Making a meal on the fly?

00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:23.434
Open, What can I make?

00:01:23.454 --> 00:01:25.384
Add anything extra you've got.

00:01:25.404 --> 00:01:27.954
Say, a can of pineapple juice.

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:30.944
Teriyaki Chicken just made the cut.

00:01:30.964 --> 00:01:33.815
Everything you can cook right now goes to the top,

00:01:33.835 --> 00:01:37.745
and the near misses tell you exactly what they're missing.

00:01:37.765 --> 00:01:39.872
Just visiting? No account needed.

00:01:39.892 --> 00:01:41.291
Type in what you have,

00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:43.586
and it works the same way.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.331
Planning a quick shopping trip for one dish?

00:01:48.351 --> 00:01:51.737
Open the recipe, and flip, Can I cook this?

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:53.606
What you have turns green.

00:01:53.626 --> 00:01:55.509
What you need turns red.

00:01:55.809 --> 00:01:58.106
For Chicken Shawarma, it's a lemon.

00:01:58.126 --> 00:02:00.050
Shopping list: done.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.560
And when nobody can decide, hit Surprise me,

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.109
and let the reel pick dinner.

00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:12.302
Dueling Kebabs.

00:02:12.322 --> 00:02:15.935
Every dish worth cooking, one menu away.

00:02:15.955 --> 00:02:17.408
Down with hunger.
